Fix: state that the template reads lives in signals,

251
00:14:42,877 --> 00:14:48,442
which schedule rendering in both modes, and DOM work after rendering uses afterNextRender or

252
00:14:48,442 --> 00:14:50,032
afterRenderEffect, never zone events.

253
00:14:51,407 --> 00:14:54,743
PERF-001 · The second team's bug: overlapping timers

254
00:14:55,868 --> 00:14:59,871
Each click starts a new timer and never cancels the previous one.

255
00:14:59,871 --> 00:15:03,207
Clicking at 0 s and 1.5 s resets the label

256
00:15:03,207 --> 00:15:06,543
at 2 s, half a second after the second click.

257
00:15:06,543 --> 00:15:09,212
The timer also survives the component being destroyed.

258
00:15:10,587 --> 00:15:14,178
PERF-001 · The second team's bug: overlapping timers

259
00:15:15,303 --> 00:15:19,252
Fix: clear the previous timer on each click, and on destroy.

260
00:15:20,627 --> 00:15:25,126
PERF-001 · Better than measuring: let CSS size the button

261
00:15:26,251 --> 00:15:29,785
Measuring the width of "Copy" and using it as min-width would

262
00:15:29,785 --> 00:15:33,319
not even work: "Copied" is longer, so the button grows anyway.

263
00:15:33,319 --> 00:15:35,890
Stack both labels in the same grid cell

264
00:15:35,890 --> 00:15:38,460
and hide the inactive one with visibility: hidden.

265
00:15:38,460 --> 00:15:41,673
The button is always as wide as the longer label,

266
00:15:41,673 --> 00:15:45,529
with no JavaScript, no layout reads, and correct behaviour when the labels

267
00:15:45,529 --> 00:15:46,171
are translated.

